WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.921
The host copies the two input arrays to

00:00:03.921 --> 00:00:06.059
GPU memory. Each array contains

00:00:06.059 --> 00:00:08.197
thirty-three float thirty-two values, and

00:00:08.197 --> 00:00:10.335
each value occupies four bytes.

00:00:14.835 --> 00:00:17.930
The host allocates the output on the GPU.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.639
Each active GPU thread reads one value

00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:23.347
from each input and writes one output.

00:00:27.847 --> 00:00:30.516
The result comes back to the CPU. Two

00:00:30.516 --> 00:00:33.184
arrays went to the GPU, and one returns.

00:00:33.184 --> 00:00:35.186
How many bytes cross between them?

00:00:43.686 --> 00:00:46.182
Each copy moves one hundred thirty-two

00:00:46.182 --> 00:00:48.678
bytes. Together, the three copies move

00:00:48.678 --> 00:00:50.342
three hundred ninety-six bytes.
